# No local plan or lot references in shipped text

Local construction plans (`Plans/`, `*_plan.md`, scratch notes) are often **out of git**.
Referencing them in shipped code, tests, or user-facing docs makes the text useless to
anyone without those files.

## Forbidden in production code, tests, README, playbooks, and `docs/`

- Mentions of « Lot N », « Lot 2.5 », « follow-up plan », « see the plan … »
- Paths like `Plans/…`, `Plans/archives/…`, filenames `*_plan.md`
- Comments / docstrings / test headers that point at a construction plan

## Allowed

- Content **inside** local plan folders only
- Agent-local notes that remind agents of this rule
- Describing **behavior** and **commands** without lot numbers

## Examples

- Bad: `// Lot 3 smoke` / `see feature_plan.md`
- Good: `Operator smoke: open the live tab, then capture` + the runnable command
